'''Monument Plaza''', also known as '''Monument Park''', was a large plaza on the populous [[ecumenopolis]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Coruscant]]. It was also the location of the planet's only uncovered [[mountain]] peak, [[Umate]], the highest point of the [[Manarai range]]. The plaza had existed for millennia, moving upward level by level as the [[city]]-world built up.

==Description==
Monument Plaza,<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> also known as Monument Park,<ref name="Into the Light">''[[The High Republic: Into the Light]]''</ref> was located on the [[ecumenopolis]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Coruscant]]. It was composed in a square and had four, large cone shaped statues which were lit<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" /> around [[Umate]], the planet's only uncovered [[mountain]] peak,<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> in the center of the park.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Shops and restaurants surrounded the plaza on all four sides,<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" /> while citizens could touch the peak itself.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" />

During the [[High Republic Era]], the park was located on [[Level 5127]] and contained substantial greenery, designed as a reflection of what the area might have looked like before it had been built over.<ref name="Light of the Jedi" />

==History==
[[File:Coruscant_Monument_Plaza.png|thumb|left|250px|Monument Plaza during the Clone Wars]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], a series of conflicts between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the breakaway [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]] and [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] secretly met in Monument Plaza when she was being pursed by the [[Coruscant Security Force|Coruscant police]] after being framed for a [[Death|murder]] she didn't commit. She gave Kenobi a [[Hologram disc|holodisc]] with a recording to be played in front of the [[Galactic Senate|Senate]] that would vindicate her.<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" /> Later in the conflict, during one of the [[Coruscant mandatory blackouts|mandatory blackouts]] following the Separatists' [[Bombing of Coruscant's central power distribution grid|bombing]] of Coruscant's [[central power distribution grid]], [[Senator]] [[Onaconda Farr]] was attacked in the plaza by [[Chata Hyoki|two]] [[Robonino|thugs]] in an attempt to deter him from opposing a [[Republic military enhancement bill|bill]] that would approve the Republic's purchase of 5 million additional [[clone trooper]]s. Later, Senator [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] made a speech in front of the Senate which was broadcast in Monument Plaza in opposition of the bill.<ref name="Pursuit of Peace">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref>

[[File:Corsectrooper.jpg|thumb|250px|Monument Plaza celebrating the death of Emperor Palpatine during the Galactic Civil War]]
During the [[Galactic Civil War]], after the [[Galactic Empire]]'s defeat by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] at the [[Battle of Endor]], a [[Uprisings against the Galactic Empire|celebration]] took place in Monument Plaza to commemorate the demise of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]. After a [[Riot in Monument Plaza|mob]] destroyed a statue of the Emperor, Coruscant Security Forces arrived at the plaza to restore order and opened fire on the crowd without warning, killing multiple civilians and transforming the celebration into a full-blown [[Riot in Monument Plaza|riot]].<ref name="Aftermath" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|In 'The Duchess of Mandalore' [sic], the plaza area in this episode was something that I had wanted to see in ''Star Wars'' since I was a kid because I knew that it was a Ralph McQuarrie painting and knew that it was something that George would be okay with if we used it. Something about it seemed so futuristic and yet a galaxy far, far away. It really felt like Coruscant with these very bizarre towers and the big monument in the middle. I'm always happy when we can give Ralph a nod. He's been so important to the overall look of ''Star Wars''. He's been such an inspiration to so many people on this show and there's nothing that I like more than bring to life some of his work.|[[Dave Filoni]] on the inclusion of Monument Plaza in "Duchess of Mandalore"|<ref name="Featurette">{{SW|url=video/duchess-of-mandalore-episode-featurette|text="Duchess of Mandalore" Episode Featurette}}</ref>}}
Monument Plaza first appeared in the [[1995]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] book ''[[The Illustrated Star Wars Universe]]'', where it was portrayed in a drawing by [[Ralph McQuarrie]] and extrapolated on in text by [[Kevin J. Anderson]]. As some of the McQuarrie art used in this book was concept art from the ''[[Star Wars]]'' movies and other pieces were commissioned for the book, with whom the idea for Monument Plaza originated is unknown.<ref name="The Illustrated Star Wars Universe">''[[The Illustrated Star Wars Universe]]''</ref> It became [[canon]] when it appeared in the [[1997]] [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]] version of [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Return of the Jedi" />

Monument Plaza's appearance in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' animated series was based on several pieces of Ralph McQuarrie concept art. The plaza also included a large boulder at its center&mdash;a nod to a detail seen in McQuarrie's work suggesting the sole exposed mountain peak on Coruscant's covered surface. Some of the original design development of this monument looked to the actual boulder found on the road to [[Lucasfilm Animation]]'s northern [[Wikipedia:California|California]] headquarters. It is this boulder that gives the Big Rock campus of [[Skywalker Ranch]] its name.<ref name="Trivia Gallery">{{SW|url=duchess-of-mandalore-trivia-gallery|text="Duchess of Mandalore" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref>

The book ''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> and the short story "''[[The Veteran]]''" from ''[[From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi]]'' places Monument Plaza on level [[Level 5,216]] of [[Coruscant]]'s [[Imperial City]].<ref name="The Veteran">{{StoryCite|story=The Veteran|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref> However, this placement contradicts several aspects of Imperial [[City]]'s established lore. Despite the [[2016]] edition of ''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|Star Wars: Complete Locations]]''<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> stating that Imperial City was made up of 5217 levels, most appearances of Imperial City since then including [[Star Wars (2020) 36|''Star Wars'' (2020) 36]]<ref name="Star Wars 36">[[Star Wars (2020) 36|''Star Wars'' (2020) 36]]</ref> and [[Star Wars Adventures (2017) 25|''Star Wars Adventures'' (2017) 25]] have consistently stated that Imperial City has 5127 levels,<ref name="The Right Wrong Turn">[[Star Wars Adventures (2017) 25|''Star Wars Adventures'' (2017) 25]]</ref> which is smaller than Level 5216. An updated version of [[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition|updated version]] of released in [[2025]] changed the number of levels in Imperial City to be 5127, and places Monument Plaza on [[Level 5127]], the highest level of the city, which this article assumes to be correct.<ref name="CLNE" />

